---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// This page is intentionally NOT linked from the main nav until the
// project is ready to publicly announce token plans. It's reachable at
// /token for direct linking only.
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Token — Atlasmc"
  description="Atlasmc is exploring a community token to fund development. No sale yet, no contract deployed, no allocation guarantees."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-10">
    <p class="inline-block text-xs font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-[var(--color-accent-bright)] mb-4">
      Status · Exploring
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Atlasmc Token</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg text-neutral-300 leading-relaxed">
      We&rsquo;re exploring a community token as a way to fund continued
      development of Atlasmc and the underlying open-source desktop app.
      Nothing has been launched. No contract is deployed. There is no
      sale, no presale, no allocation, and no investment opportunity at
      this time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pb-16 space-y-8">
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-bg-elevated)] p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">What we&rsquo;re considering</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[var(--color-accent)] space-y-2 text-neutral-300 text-sm">
        <li>A utility token tied to the Atlasmc project &mdash; not a security and not an investment.</li>
        <li>Treasury funding for development, infrastructure (hosted generator, tile caches), and community grants.</li>
        <li>Lightweight on-chain governance for non-critical project decisions.</li>
        <li>Transparent vesting and unlock schedule, published before any sale.</li>
        <li>Independent smart-contract audit before any deployment.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-bg-elevated)] p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">What it is not</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[var(--color-accent)] space-y-2 text-neutral-300 text-sm">
        <li>A precondition for using the desktop app. Atlasmc the application will always be free, open source, and Apache-2.0.</li>
        <li>Required to generate worlds, download releases, or contribute code.</li>
        <li>An offering of securities. Holders should not expect profit derived from the efforts of others.</li>
        <li>Endorsed by, affiliated with, or representative of upstream Arnis or Louis Erbkamm.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-bg-elevated)] p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Updates</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        All token-related announcements will go through the
        <a href="https://github.com/kodekaze1/atlasmc" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[var(--color-accent-bright)] underline">GitHub repository</a>
        first. Watch the repo for tagged releases and discussions. If we
        publish a whitepaper, audit report, or transparency dashboard,
        they will be linked here and from the project README before any
        sale. Anyone claiming an &ldquo;official Atlasmc presale&rdquo; on Telegram,
        Discord, X, or anywhere else without a corresponding release on
        this site and the GitHub repo is a scam &mdash; treat it as such.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-bg-elevated)] p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Disclaimer</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Cryptocurrency tokens carry significant risk and may be classified
        as securities in your jurisdiction. Nothing on this page is
        financial, legal, or tax advice. Consult a licensed professional
        in your country before participating in any token-related
        activity. Atlasmc and its maintainers will not be liable for
        decisions made based on this page&rsquo;s content. This page may be
        updated as the project&rsquo;s plans change.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
